# Local secrets.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored; this template is the checked-in copy. Loaded automatically by the API at
# start-up, by the test suite, and by docker compose for variable substitution — so nothing here
# needs exporting into your shell.
#
# Secrets only. Anything that is an address, a port, a label, or a value every developer sets
# identically is configuration, not a secret, and belongs in source control:
#
#   * application settings  -> src/Lakehold.Api/appsettings*.json  (telemetry, CDC, maintenance)
#   * service ports/users   -> compose.yaml, which carries its own defaults
#
# Keeping this file small is the point: the shorter it is, the easier it is to see that everything
# in it genuinely had to be kept out of the repository.
#
# These particular values are throwaway credentials for local containers on loopback ports. Replacing
# them is optional locally and mandatory anywhere else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backing service credentials (read by compose.yaml)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=lakehold
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=lakehold123

# Required by the application. The control plane and DuckLake metadata may use separate PostgreSQL
# databases/users in production; local development uses the same database with isolated schemas.
ConnectionStrings__ControlPlane=Host=localhost;Port=55439;Database=lakeholdmeta;Username=lakehold;Password=lakehold
ConnectionStrings__DuckLakeMetadata=Host=localhost;Port=55439;Database=lakeholdmeta;Username=lakehold;Password=lakehold

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration tests
#
# Each suite is gated on its variable and skips when unset, so `dotnet test` needs no services by
# default. Filling these in is what opts you into running them — after `docker compose up -d`.
# Comment a block out to go back to skipping it.
#
# The non-secret half of each block (endpoint, bucket) lives here rather than in appsettings because
# the tests read the process environment directly, and because the gate only means anything
# alongside the credential it authenticates with.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PostgreSQL-backed catalog metadata. A libpq connection string, not a .NET one.
LAKEHOLD_TEST_POSTGRES=Host=localhost;Port=55439;Database=lakeholdmeta;Username=lakehold;Password=lakehold

# S3-compatible object store. The bucket is created by the minio-bucket service in compose.yaml;
# the tests assume it already exists and do not create it.
LAKEHOLD_TEST_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:59000
LAKEHOLD_TEST_S3_KEY=lakehold
LAKEHOLD_TEST_S3_SECRET=lakehold123
LAKEHOLD_TEST_S3_BUCKET=lakehold-test

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application secrets
#
# Double underscore is the .NET configuration separator: Lakehouse__EjectSigningKey binds to
# Lakehouse:EjectSigningKey.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Signs eject manifests with HMAC-SHA256, making the row-count and digest attestation
# tamper-evident. Unset leaves bundles unsigned but still digest-attested. This is a real secret:
# it must never reach a manifest, a response, or a log.
# Lakehouse__EjectSigningKey=change-me-to-something-random

# The shared password for the PostgreSQL wire endpoint (Lakehold:PgWire:Enabled). It is what Power
# BI, Tableau, and psql present, and it authenticates every tenant, so it is as sensitive as the
# catalogs the node serves. Enabling the endpoint without setting this refuses to start — see
# docs/POSTGRES-WIRE.md.
# Lakehold__PgWire__Password=change-me-to-something-random

# Preferred over the shared password above on a multi-tenant node: a per-tenant secret authenticates
# that tenant only, whereas the shared one authenticates the connection but not the tenant it named.
# When any of these are set they are authoritative and the shared password is ignored.
# Lakehold__PgWire__TenantPasswords__demo=change-me-to-something-random

# Password protecting the wire endpoint's TLS certificate, when it is a protected PKCS#12 bundle.
# Lakehold__PgWire__TlsCertificatePassword=change-me

# Preferred over both of the above: with Lakehold:PgWire:AllowTokenAuthentication set, BI clients
# present a Lakehold API token instead, verified against the same store the HTTP API uses — so
# revoking a credential closes both surfaces at once. Tokens are issued through the API, not
# configured here; there is no secret to put in this file. The setting itself is not a secret and
# belongs in appsettings. Note that it requires TLS, because a hashed token store cannot answer
# PostgreSQL's MD5 challenge — see docs/POSTGRES-WIRE.md.

# The first instance-scoped API token, for platforms that inject credentials rather than reading the
# one the API mints and logs once on an empty node. Must be a well-formed lkh_admin_… token. It
# provisions tenants, catalogs, and tokens, and deliberately cannot read data.
# Lakehold__BootstrapToken=lkh_admin_change-me-to-something-random

# Object-storage examples. Set Lakehouse__DataRoot to a bucket/prefix, choose the default profile,
# then supply the matching profile credentials. Catalogs can override the profile by name.
#
# Lakehouse__DataRoot=s3://my-bucket/lakehold
# Lakehouse__DefaultStorageProfile=primary
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Kind=S3
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__KeyId=change-me
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Secret=change-me
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Region=eu-west-1
#
# Lakehouse__DataRoot=gs://my-bucket/lakehold
# Lakehouse__DefaultStorageProfile=primary
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Kind=Gcs
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__KeyId=gcs-hmac-access-id
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Secret=gcs-hmac-secret
#
# Lakehouse__DataRoot=az://my-container/lakehold
# Lakehouse__DefaultStorageProfile=primary
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__Kind=Azure
# Lakehouse__StorageProfiles__primary__AzureConnectionString=change-me
